WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.690
We operated on him too late

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.230
to reverse the damage to his optic nerves.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:07.610
It's a miracle that some of his optic nerves

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.110
are still intact.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:11.690
But I...

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:17.660
had no idea how much pain he was in.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.540
He wasn't hurting just because he had lost his eyesight,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.920
but also because he knew that he couldn't go back to you without his eyes.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:32.050
That's why he was in pain.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:35.760
And so was Ms. Mi Hee, who stood by his side watching.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:40.310
She kept blaming herself,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:41.950
saying because she lied,

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.390
Joonsang had lost his vision and you.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:45.850
She lied?

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:51.570
I thought she lied, saying that you two had the same father?

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.440
What do you mean, "She lied"?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.260
Are you sure you're not mistaken?

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:56.860
We're...

00:00:58.950 --> 00:00:59.870
brother and sister.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.870
You mean you didn't know this whole time?

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:09.080
You and Joonsang are not related.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.750
Joonsang's father is...

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.100
Where are you going?

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:52.770
On a trip.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.770
By yourself?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.780
Don't worry, I'm used to it now.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:11.040
Thanks for everything.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.290
It must've been difficult dealing with a menacing patient like me.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.430
Think of it as a vacation.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.630
I'll be back to menace you some more when I return.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:23.510
You <i>have</i> to come back, okay?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.100
Of course.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.100
Oh yeah, can you hold on to these for me?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.940
Give 'em back to me when I return.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.320
I will.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.320
Oh yeah, I have a present for you.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:42.910
A present?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.330
What's this?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.630
Give this to Yujin, okay?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:56.840
I...

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:02.460
You <i>must</i> give it to her.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:03.630
You have to meet her, okay?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:07.850
Promise me.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.270
I hope she likes it.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.000
He hasn't called me once since he left.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.290
I don't know where he went or where he is now.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.710
So I guess he kept his promise about building "The Impossible House."

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:27.340
I wanted him to go back to you.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.650
Joonsang was quite a handful, wasn't he?

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.730
You don't need to worry anymore.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.270
I'm going to find him.

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.320
I'll search every corner of the earth

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:49.740
if I have to.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.640
<i>I'm not scared of anything anymore.</i>

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.680
<i>I'm really not, as long as I have you.</i>

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.350
<i>As long as I have you by my side.</i>

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:20.520
<i>And that's why...</i>

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.480
<i>I'm tired and hurting right now.</i>

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.120
<i>Because I'm scared I may never find you,</i>

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.780
<i>and never see you again.</i>

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.590
Over here, Mama.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.580
Here you go.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.330
Thank you.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.420
And this is <i>my</i> gift to you.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.020
Thanks, lady!

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:11.300
<i>Maybe...</i>

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.300
<i>life is just one big puzzle.</i>

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.810
<i>Except...</i>

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.350
<i>the difference between life and those puzzles you like so much,</i>

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.460
<i>is that life is an imperfect puzzle</i>

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.690
<i>that's been missing a few pieces from the beginning.</i>

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:28.700
<i>They say...</i>

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:31.940
<i>when God created this world and gave us this puzzle called "life,"</i>

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:37.160
<i>he took out some of the pieces, leaving us an imperfect game.</i>

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.290
<i>What should I do,</i>

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:46.080
<i>if the puzzle piece that God took out of my life</i>

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:48.750
<i>turns out to be...</i>

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.050
<i>you?</i>

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:56.970
Could I see your ticket, please?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.180
Thank you.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:08.100
The designs for the Impossible House were a failure.

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:12.360
No, the house was impossible to begin with.

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.850
You said that a loving heart

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:18.450
is the best home that two loving people could have, didn't you?

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:22.160
And that you wanted to build a house with all the warmth of one.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.610
Welcome aboard.

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.340
May I see your ticket?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:38.640
Welcome aboard.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.310
Are you all right, sir?

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:50.360
Are you all right?

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.700
Would you like a newspaper?

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:06.410
Newspaper?

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:07.660
I'll take one.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.920
<i>If I keep on filling in the puzzle,</i>

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:15.630
<i>maybe I'll find out whether you really are the missing piece.</i>

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:19.470
<i>I'm going to try my best, Joonsang.</i>

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.850
<i>So don't give up on me.</i>

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.030
No!

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.420
I'm sorry.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:02.720
This young man started joking around, so I unwittingly...

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:04.970
Hey!

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.470
You're the one who started—

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.100
Apologize to the man!

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:08.930
It's all right.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.730
More importantly, which way is the asylum?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.230
Come again?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.960
I'm here to visit Ms. Mi Hee Kang,

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:20.030
who's currently staying at the asylum.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.740
There is indeed a woman staying at the asylum right now.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.540
Where is it?

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.370
Could you take me there?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.120
What's going on here?

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:39.050
I'm looking for Ms. Mi Hee Kang.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.740
How did you know I was here?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.770
I asked Manager Kim to let me know

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.950
as soon as he found out where you were.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.190
What brought you all the way out here?

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:16.750
If you're looking for Joonsang, I don't know where he is either.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.340
I'm not here just for Joonsang.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.880
You think it's all your fault, don't you?

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.930
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.350
Do you know what sets people in love apart from others?

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:38.770
They unconditionally believe everything their partner says.

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.320
Hyeonsoo may have left you,

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.070
but he never stopped loving you.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.240
I'm taking the picture now.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.290
Make it a good one, okay?

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:55.790
Come on, hurry up!

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.250
Why don't you get in the picture too, Kyeonghee?

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.260
Yeah, I'll take the next one.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.370
Here I go.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.440
I'd better look pretty in it!

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:09.120
All right.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:09.800
Let's take one more.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.020
Come over here for a bit, Hyeonsoo.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.310
Hold on.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.060
Are you two going out or something?

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:19.610
Why? Do we make a good couple?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.530
I thought you didn't like having your picture taken?

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:32.740
I just felt like it.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:34.830
What?

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:37.040
Today's a special day, after all.

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:42.250
Why did you want to be in a picture with us?

00:13:50.180 --> 00:13:52.100
Ride in front. I'll teach you.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.100
What's gotten into you?

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.100
You've been asking me to teach you, right?

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.620
If you don't want to fall, keep pedaling.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:13.580
That's all I have to do?

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.870
Also, turn the handle if you think you're going to fall.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.750
Turn towards the direction you're falling.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:21.630
Anything else?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.930
Just keep pedaling.

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:26.630
You'll get used to it.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.100
Oh my God, I've got it!

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.090
I'm doing well, aren't I?

00:14:41.090 --> 00:14:42.480
Don't let go yet!

00:14:42.810 --> 00:14:45.150
You can ride by yourself now, right?

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.420
Let's break up.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:04.000
What?

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.920
No, we can't.

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:22.310
This is ridiculous...

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.780
Why aren't you saying anything?

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:40.200
Mi Hee told you what happened, didn't she?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.310
Would you stop being so upset?

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:53.340
I thought you'd accepted that Mi Hee's parents don't want you to see her.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:58.140
I'm not upset, and it's not because of her parents.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.350
It's all my fault.

00:16:01.230 --> 00:16:04.350
It's not too late to call her and tell her that you're sorry.

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:05.860
That you didn't mean it.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:07.820
But I <i>did</i> mean it.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:09.570
You saw her today.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.030
It was her first performance as a rising new pianist.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.190
I guess it wouldn't matter much if she was dating you,

00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:16.410
because you're a graduate student.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.240
You have your art though.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:23.830
I just got rejected by the national competition for the umpteenth time.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.090
I don't have the talent or the time to keep doing this.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.590
Mi Hee will become pathetic if she stays by my side.

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:35.890
You should've been the one who dated her from the start.

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.300
What are you talking about?

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:41.390
You like Mi Hee, don't you?

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:56.910
"The First Time"?

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:01.700
It's that song I kept humming, remember?

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.960
Yeah, you wanted to transcribe it and give it to Mi Hee as a present, right?

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:11.840
"The First Time"...

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:13.340
I see.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.340
Give that to Mi Hee for me.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:32.030
I couldn't bring myself to tell you

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.180
why Hyeonsoo broke up with you and wanted to get married so quickly,

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:37.530
even though I knew all along.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:41.280
Joonsang asked me,

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:46.660
why his father left him, and what happened between you two.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:51.380
Back then, I was so sure that Hyeonsoo was his father.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.340
I'm the one who lied to him. You shouldn't be hung up about it.

00:17:57.720 --> 00:18:00.260
No, it's all my fault.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:02.760
Jinwoo...

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:07.560
Joonsang, Yujin, and even Sanghyuk...

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:12.610
Where did we go wrong?

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:50.190
I, Hyeonsoo Jung, solemnly swear to love and honor Kyeonghee Kim forever.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:55.730
I, Kyeonghee Kim, solemnly swear to love and honor Hyeonsoo Jung forever.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:19:00.360
You have now declared your vows before the Church.

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:52.750
Mi Hee!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.210
What are you doing?

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:15.650
Hyeonsoo...

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:20.320
Hyeonsoo!

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.150
Out of my way!

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:25.160
Hyeonsoo. Hyeonsoo!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.580
Don't leave me, Hyeonsoo!

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.330
Let me go.{filled in from jp sub}

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:37.250
Don't be like this.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:39.820
Our relationship is like cracked glass.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.180
All it can do now is shatter.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.220
Hyeonsoo!

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.630
No, Hyeonsoo!

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.720
Don't leave me!

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.350
Come back!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.730
Are you all right?

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:39.150
How do you know this song?

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:43.820
Boy, was I surprised.

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.820
I never thought I'd meet the world-renowned pianist Mi Hee Kang here.

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:50.250
I was the one who was surprised.

00:21:50.250 --> 00:21:51.830
You played so wonderfully.

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:56.460
I was dumbstruck when I heard you play in Paris ten years ago.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:02.130
Ever since then, I've practiced "The First Time" day in and day out.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.050
I see.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:06.840
That song actually gave me a miracle.

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.550
A miracle, you say?

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:14.520
Thanks to this song, I met someone

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:17.390
who reunited me with my lost wife and son.

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:23.570
That's the second time he's experienced "the Miracle of the Basilica."

00:22:24.610 --> 00:22:25.530
They're right.

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:27.110
It's all thanks to her.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:31.870
Could you please elaborate on your story?

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:33.910
Monsieur Claude?

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:38.410
I'm sorry. I didn't realize you had guests.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:40.300
Oh no, you came just in time.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:42.380
I was just about to tell them about Yujin.

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:47.130
Did you just say, "Yujin"?

00:22:47.760 --> 00:22:50.300
Yes, she was from Korea, just like you.

00:22:51.340 --> 00:22:53.010
Here's a picture of her.

00:22:59.020 --> 00:22:59.940
My God...
